Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:10:06

Added. Covers from SteamGridDB for the portrait in Steam's library (owner, 22-10-2026), with core's covers. A PSP
game has no 2:3 picture of its own, so the portrait was always drawn from its icon and title. With the suite's
SteamGridDB API key, entered under the new Covers… button (one key for every app of the suite), Update Game Mode
first looks each ticked game up by its title and takes the portrait with the most votes. Only the portrait: the wide
picture, the banner and the logo stay the game's own. What is found is kept in
~/.local/share/bc250-ppsspp-manager/covers under the game's disc ID, so it is not asked for again; a game in Steam
not yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network stops the lookup with a message and the
drawn portrait is used; the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key nothing changes. The artwork is now
drawn in the background job, after the lookup. install.sh --uninstall --purge removes the covers folder too; the installer test checks it. Test: the cover in place of the drawn portrait, and Covers… with
Update Game Mode in the window, SteamGridDB's answers made in the test.

